            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-WsAyduyX2o61ZHxXZcmlo6dggBd\">The line graph gives information about the proportion of people of different age groups going to the movies at least one time per month from 1984 to 2003.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13661,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 234,
            "sort": 2,
            "name": "Overview",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-UObNdEjpeoatWExGQgCliu0ugKd\">Overall, it is clear that the popularity of going to the cinema went up during the period shown among all four age brackets, with the 15-24 group doing so the most, while those above 35 years old had the least interest.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13661,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 235,
            "sort": 3,
            "name": "Body 1",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div>Looking at younger individuals, in 1984, around 18% of those from 15 to 24 had the habit of visiting the cinema, far higher than the youngest group, 7-14, at 10%. An upward trend was recorded for the former group, with its figures rising to around 32% in 1992, before fluctuating and peaking at approximately 57% in 2003. A similar increasing tendency was seen in the 7-14 age bracket, as the numbers rose to 18% in 1992, continued climbing to reach 30% in 2003.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13661,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 236,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"N0Dfd70vKo3C16x22MllfNEwg8e\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-WbIYdS25hogu6LxX9gHlUuO8gkf\">Regarding the other groups, there were around 4% of 25-to-35-year-olds and 1% of people older than that going to the cinema at least once a month in 1984. The younger bracket's numbers increased significantly to a quarter (25%) in 2003, despite some fluctuations from 1996 to 2000, while those for the older group did so far less significantly, rising to only about 12% in 2003.</div>\n</div>",
            "question_id": 13661,
            "is_toggle_on": true
          }
        ],
